Chimera's port of the fork's Bink 2 decoder to FFmpeg 7.1 (wasm/bink2/build.sh
applies it, after the fixes, to the fork's three decoder files copied into
FFmpeg 7.1's source).

Registration, as the fork's commit adding the decoder did it: a codec ID
(AV_CODEC_ID_BINKVIDEO2, at the end of the video IDs), its descriptor, the
codec list, the Makefile and configure.

bink2.c, for what changed in FFmpeg's internals between 2022 and 7.1:
- headers: ff_get_buffer and ff_set_dimensions are in decode.h; the memory
  functions, DECLARE_ALIGNED and emms_c come from their own libavutil headers;
- a keyframe is marked with AV_FRAME_FLAG_KEY, not frame->key_frame;
- the code tables use the VLC API that replaced ff_init_vlc_sparse (VLCElem
  entries, VLC_INIT_* flags), and are built once for all decoders (with
  ff_thread_once, as other decoders do) instead of on every open, the
  FF_CODEC_CAP_INIT_THREADSAFE flag they relied on being gone;
- ff_blockdsp_init takes no codec context;
- CODEC_LONG_NAME for the long name.

Nothing that decodes changes: 83 of the Remastered Collection's movies (80
with alpha) give the same frames, every one, as the fork with the same fixes.

